{
  "requirement": "The SDK supplies a filesystem-backed helper for the `load_evidence` and\n`store_evidence` methods under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. An application can\ndelegate to that helper when implementing `EvidenceStorage`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has two obligations. The SDK must supply a filesystem-backed helper for `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`. An application must be able to delegate to that helper when implementing `EvidenceStorage`.\n\nThe marked test `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs#fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]` covers both obligations:\n- **Helper is supplied:** the test uses the SDK's `FileEvidenceStorage`. It also uses `FileStorageError` as the `EvidenceStorage` error type.\n- **Delegation works:** `impl[StoredGraph/EvidenceStorage]` implements `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` by calling `self.0.load(&self.node_path(node))` and `self.0.store(...)`. The test drives the trait methods on this consumer type.\n- **Behavior through the delegate:**\n  - Loading an unstored node returns `Ok(None)`.\n  - Storing a record and then loading it returns the same `dependencies` and `output`. The node id is `opaque/é`, a non-path-safe key.\n  - Loading a different node returns `None`.\n  - Corrupt JSON on disk makes `load_evidence` return `Err(FileStorageError::Json(_))`.\n\nThe test does not assert `procedure` after the delegated round trip. The subject text does not require it. The procedure-preservation clause belongs to `evidence_storage`, which the subject only cites, and to the separate `filesystem-storage.store` requirement. That requirement is tested in `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]`, which asserts `saved.procedure == \"v1\"`. The helper's detailed behavior is therefore not this subject's concern.\n\nI found no gap in test adequacy for this requirement.",
  "references": "a7acd7515cb0da8eb4bcf8d281a19c2b8af40b6a81e09f15ac3b27df2c4034e1",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage.filesystem",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage.filesystem"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage.filesystem",
        "The SDK supplies a filesystem-backed helper for the `load_evidence` and",
        "`store_evidence` methods under",
        "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. An application can",
        "delegate to that helper when implementing `EvidenceStorage`.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} evidence_storage",
        "The application implements this trait from `habeas_sdk::graph`:",
        "",
        "```rust,ignore",
        "use std::future::Future;",
        "",
        "pub trait EvidenceStorage: Graph {",
        "    /// Look up a node's record. Ok(None) means absent; Err means storage failed.",
        "    /// The node identity is the key, with no separate procedure-name key.",
        "    fn load_evidence<'a>(",
        "        &'a self,",
        "        node: &'a Self::NodeId,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<",
        "        Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::JudgmentMetadata, Self::EdgeLabel>>,",
        "        Self::Error,",
        "    >> + Send + 'a;",
        "",
        "    /// Save the complete record, preserving its procedure version,",
        "    /// dependencies, and judgment.",
        "    fn store_evidence<'a>(",
        "        &'a self,",
        "        node: &'a Self::NodeId,",
        "        record: &'a Record<Self::NodeId, Self::JudgmentMetadata, Self::EdgeLabel>,",
        "    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send + 'a;",
        "}",
        "```",
        "",
        "The runner passes the requested node identity directly to these methods.",
        "The application chooses the persistence mechanism; the interface requires",
        "neither filesystem paths nor a global listing of evidence.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
